# FIXED 2026-10-11 (experiments/2026-10-11-libraries3/README.md); kept as the record of the bug.
# `&.` is listed as rejected (cheatsheet "Also rejected"), but the chain form `x&.T.op` is accepted and
# runs as `x.T.op`: no nil short-circuit. Expected: rejected before running (exit 2), or Ruby's `&.`.
# Observed: --strict=1 runs it and fails at line 7 with TypeError (String.size got nil);
# with a non-nil type (line 6) it is silently the same as `.`.
def maybe(n) = n > 0 ? "abc" : nil
p("abc"&.String.size)
p(maybe(0)&.String.size)
